{"path":"utility/functional/mem_fun_ref","title":"std::mem_fun_ref","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>mem_fun_ref","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Creates a member function wrapper object, deducing the target type from the template arguments. The wrapper object expects a reference to an object of type T as the first parameter to its operator().","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/functional\">&lt;functional&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Res, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2743\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mem_fun_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Res,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> mem_fun_ref<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Res <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Res, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2745\">std::<span class=\"me2\">const_mem_fun_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Res,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> mem_fun_ref<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Res <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Res, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Arg <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2744\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mem_fun1_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Res,T,Arg<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> mem_fun_ref<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Res <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>Arg<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Res, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Arg <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2746\">std::<span class=\"me2\">const_mem_fun1_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Res,T,Arg<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> mem_fun_ref<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Res <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>Arg<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Creates a member function wrapper object, deducing the target type from the template arguments. The wrapper object expects a reference to an object of type <code>T</code> as the first parameter to its <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2743\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mem_fun_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>S,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2745\">std::<span class=\"me2\">const_mem_fun_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>S,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2744\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mem_fun1_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>S,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun_ref_t\"><span class=\"kw2746\">std::<span class=\"me2\">const_mem_fun1_ref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>S,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>This function and the related types were deprecated in C++11 and removed in C++17 in favor of the more general <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fn\">std::mem_fn</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/bind\">std::bind</a></span>, both of which create callable adaptor-compatible function objects from member functions.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> f\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to a member function to create a wrapper for\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A function object wrapping <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>May throw implementation-defined exceptions. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The difference between <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun\"><span class=\"kw2742\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mem_fun</span></span></a></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mem_fun_ref</span></span></code> is that the former produces a function wrapper that expects a pointer to an object, whereas the latter — a reference.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>Uses <code>std::mem_fun_ref</code> to bind <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\">std::string</a></span>'s member function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/size\">size()</a></span>.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;functional&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iterator&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;vector&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"once\"</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"upon\"</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"a\"</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"time\"</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/transform\"><span class=\"kw1601\">std::<span class=\"me2\">transform</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v.<span class=\"me1\">cbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, v.<span class=\"me1\">cend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n                   <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ostream_iterator\"><span class=\"kw675\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostream_iterator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a>, <span class=\"st0\">\" \"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n                   std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mem_fun_ref</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">string</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>4 4 1 4</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/mem_fun\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>mem_fun</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-deprecated-cxx11\">(deprecated in C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates a wrapper from a pointer to member function, callable with a pointer to object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/functional","title":"Function objects"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::mem_fun_ref","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++17. Creates a member function wrapper object, deducing the target type from the template arguments."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"f"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A function object wrapping f."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw implementation-defined exceptions."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The difference between std::mem_fun and std::mem_fun_ref is that the former produces a function wrapper that expects a pointer to an object, whereas the…"},{"label":"Example","note":"Uses std::mem_fun_ref to bind std::string's member function size()."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"mem_fun","note":"creates a wrapper from a pointer to member function, callable with a pointer to object"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17"],"wordCount":277,"codeBlockCount":2}
